@startuml
title SIC/XE Simulator - Run Until Stop
actor Frontend
participant Client
participant WebSocketServer as WS
participant Simulator
participant CPU as "Architecture / CPU"

Frontend -> Client : run()
Client -> WS : Run request
WS -> Simulator : run()

loop until breakpoint / halt / input
  Simulator -> CPU : execute instruction
  CPU --> Simulator : events/state
  Simulator -> Simulator : check stop condition
end

CPU --> Simulator : stopped
Simulator --> WS : final execution result
WS --> Client : response
Client --> Frontend : resolve(result)

note over Simulator,CPU
Run is optimized for continuous execution.
The frontend does not need every intermediate
visual state unless the implementation chooses
to stream execution events.
end note

@enduml
